      "side": 1,
      "message": "This commit is useful for the following case:\n\nThe kernel is using the \u0027type\u0027 field in order to know during driver probe whether a port is dedicated or is USB. If we boot from the dedicated port, then everything is fine, because the kernel driver will receive \u0027type \u003d\u003d USB_CHG_TYPE_DEDICATED\u0027 and will be able to create the sysfs entry accordingly.\nBut if the device was booted from USB, then the kernel driver will receive USB_CHG_TYPE_NONE and will not be able to distinguish whether the port is USB or dedicated.",
